WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.020
There stands a good chance that Avengers:
Endgame might mark the final film for several

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:09.080
Marvel favorites, but in the weeks leading
up to the film's launch, the cast is keeping

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.060
their minds off such grim outcomes.

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:15.480
The Endgame press tour has been filled with
both laughter and emotional moments.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.420
However, there's no escaping the fact that
the end is nigh, and that Earth's Mightiest

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:21.920
Heroes will face a dangerous fight in Endgame.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:26.380
One member of the Endgame team who isn't letting
the rest of the cast forget that harrowing

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:31.569
reality is none other than Thanos actor Josh
Brolin, who has delivered a terrifying reminder

00:00:31.569 --> 00:00:33.220
to his fellow MCU stars.

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:37.980
Taking to Instagram, Brolin posted a photo
of a set chair with the Mad Titan's name written

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:41.960
on it, plus the Infinity Gauntlet carefully
sitting atop the seat's back.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.220
He wrote in the caption:

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:48.040
"When you all are done with all your interviews
and your talk shows, I'll slip this perfectly

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:51.700
fitting gauntlet back on and tell you a story
about your future."

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:53.180
"He's pretty good at that."

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:53.800
"Right?"

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:59.400
Just as Brolin's post hints, the Avengers:
Endgame crew has been incredibly busy promoting

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.340
the ensemble pic.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:05.200
What they haven't been able to do during those
events is, ironically, talk about what's coming

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.840
in Endgame, if they even know themselves.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.640
"I didn't even get a whole script to this
movie.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:11.940
I don't know why.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.380
The script I did get had dummy scenes in it."

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:21.640
Marvel is keeping an airtight lid on Endgame
details, and for good reason, as the studio

00:01:21.659 --> 00:01:26.219
doesn't want to ruin the movie-going experience
for anyone or risk damaging what's meant to

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:30.200
be the culmination of 11 years of stories
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.600
That said, the interviews the Endgame stars
are giving are essentially hype-boosters rather

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:37.020
than detail-dishings.

00:01:37.189 --> 00:01:41.380
In some ways, the lack of plot specifics and
the hesitancy to talk too much about Endgame

00:01:41.389 --> 00:01:45.740
is a distraction from the inevitable: the
un-dusted heroes are all but guaranteed to

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:48.000
go head-to-head with Thanos once more.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:49.980
Still, everyone knows that's coming.

00:01:49.999 --> 00:01:53.779
The Endgame teasers, specifically the most
recent special-look trailer, point toward

00:01:53.779 --> 00:01:58.329
the Avengers crafting a plan to take down
the Mad Titan, reverse his Decimation, and

00:01:58.329 --> 00:02:03.369
resurrect the fallen heroes, plus the billions
upon billions of other lives that were lost

00:02:03.369 --> 00:02:04.200
post-snap.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:07.200
What that mission entails is a total mystery,
though.

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:11.530
A theory that has gained more traction than
others is that the team will gear up in their

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:15.820
new suits, which look kinda similar to the
one Hank Pym wore in the Quantum Realm in

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:20.450
Ant-Man and the Wasp, and travel back in time
to stop Thanos from ever coming close to getting

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:22.040
his hands on the Infinity Gauntlet.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:27.140
Another notion is grounded in something Captain
Marvel said in the latest look at Endgame:

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.360
"So let's get 'em.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:30.980
Use them to bring everyone back."

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:31.840
"Just like that?"

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:32.600
"Yeah."

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:37.800
The heroes may not turn back the clock, but
may instead remain in the existing timeline,

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:42.020
journeying through space to rip the Infinity
Stones straight from Thanos' hand.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:46.180
Speaking of the Infinity Gauntlet, there's
also the idea that the mystical armored glove

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:50.340
won't be as powerful in Endgame as it was
in the final moments of Infinity War, which

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:54.480
saw both the Gauntlet and Thanos' arm suffer
damage as a result of the Snap.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:59.330
The glimpses at Endgame we've gotten so far
hint that the Gauntlet is charred, and the

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:01.680
Russo brothers previously revealed that, quote,

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:09.640
"The power that it takes to use all six stones
is significant and clearly damaged the gauntlet

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.060
and damaged Thanos."

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:16.670
Joe Russo added during a Q&amp;A session following
a screening of Infinity War that Thanos' arm

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:21.860
is burned, and explained that the damage extends
to other parts of his body, including anything

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:23.980
that's on his arm, like the Infinity Gauntlet.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:25.220
Russo said:

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:30.740
"The physical price is the extreme power that
it took to enact his plan, he paid for physically,

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:34.420
and when he sits down on the steps at the
end of the movie you can see that it actually

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:36.940
carries up into his neck and onto his face.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:40.980
His arm is f---ed up and anything attached
to his arm is f---ed up."

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:46.140
So even though Thanos will evidently slip
the Gauntlet back on and spin a terrifying

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:51.040
tale about what his vision of the future holds
for the heroes he didn't kill in his Decimation,

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:55.100
there's a chance that the damage he has already
done to the Gauntlet and to his own body will

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:58.420
throw a wrench in his overall plan, whatever
that may be.

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:03.970
Right now, the ratio of answered questions
to unsolved mysteries surrounding Avengers:

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:07.920
Endgame is pretty low, and no matter how hard
we speculate about what could happen in the

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:11.960
film, the only way to get the truth is to
wait patiently until the film opens in theaters

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.330
on April 26.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:14.860
You know what that means.

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:16.780
"We're in the endgame now."

